# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Login
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The passcode typed on the login screen. If unset, the app falls back to
# "elite" and warns you on the login page. Set this before deploying.
BCC_PASSCODE=change-me

# Signs the session cookie. Any long random string: openssl rand -hex 32
BCC_SESSION_SECRET=change-me-too

# Optional second passcode that opens a DEMO board instead of the live one:
# a generated pipeline of ~77 projects for showing the product, stored
# separately, refreshed daily, and completely invisible to the live board.
# Leave unset and demo access does not exist.
# BCC_DEMO_PASSCODE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage — optional locally, REQUIRED for any hosted deployment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE of the two. Without either, the app writes ./data/db.json, which is
# fine on your own machine and is wiped on every deploy on a real host.
#
# 1. Own server (Coolify, Docker, a VPS) — point this at a mounted volume.
#    This is all you need; there is no external database to run.
# BCC_DATA_DIR=/data
#
# 2. Serverless (Vercel) — Redis, because there is no disk. Whatever your
#    provider injects when you connect a database to the project will be read;
#    you should not need to paste anything by hand.
#
#    REST (Upstash, Vercel KV) — preferred on serverless, no connection to keep
#    alive between invocations:
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
#
#    TCP (Redis Cloud, Coolify's Redis service, any self-hosted server):
# REDIS_URL=redis://...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email intake — forward a bid invitation and it lands on the board
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared secret your mail provider sends with each inbound webhook, as
# ?token=... or an x-bcc-token header. Until this is set the inbound endpoint
# refuses everything — it never accepts anonymous writes. This is the real
# guard on the door; the sender rules below only choose which board.
# BCC_INBOUND_SECRET=

# Approved senders normally live IN THE APP — Data & backup → Email intake — so
# setting up another account is a form rather than a redeploy. This variable is
# the fallback, checked after them, and is useful for bootstrapping or for
# keeping one address permanently allowed whatever the data says.
#
# Comma-separated. Each entry is an address or an "@domain", optionally "=live"
# or "=demo" (live if omitted).
#
# With no approved senders anywhere, every sender routes to the live board —
# which is what a brand new deployment needs to receive its first email at all.
# BCC_INBOUND_SENDERS=you@yourdomain.com, @yourdomain.com
#
# Set to accept mail from senders that match nothing above — for instance if
# you put bids@ on a bid tab and GCs email it directly. Unset means refuse.
# BCC_INBOUND_DEFAULT_WORKSPACE=live

# Reads the forwarded email and fills in the project fields. Without a key the
# app falls back to plain text matching, which still catches dates, dollar
# amounts, and materials but flags itself as low confidence.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
# BCC_EXTRACTION_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Confirmation replies — whoever forwards an email gets one back saying what
# landed, what was read out of it, and what is worth checking. They need
# RESEND_API_KEY and BCC_NOTIFY_FROM below (the same ones the digest uses), and
# are switched on per board under Data & backup → Email intake.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Morning follow-up digest — optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One email each weekday listing what is overdue, due today, active with no
# next action booked, and which bids close this week. Every row links straight
# to the project. It is skipped entirely on a day with nothing to say.
#
# Sent through Resend (https://resend.com — free tier covers this easily).
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# BCC_NOTIFY_EMAIL=taylor@eliteroofing.com     # comma-separate for several
# BCC_NOTIFY_FROM=Bid Command Center <bids@yourdomain.com>
#
# Secret the scheduler presents. Vercel Cron sends it automatically once set;
# without it the scheduled endpoint refuses to run at all.
# CRON_SECRET=
#
# How many days ahead the "Coming up" section looks. Default 7.
# BCC_DIGEST_LOOKAHEAD_DAYS=7

# Where the email's links should point. Vercel fills this in on its own; set it
# only when running somewhere else, or behind a custom domain.
# BCC_APP_URL=https://bids.eliteroofing.com
